1
00:00:00,143 --> 00:00:02,543
Hephaestus turned back before Lemnos.

2
00:00:02,594 --> 00:00:05,592
He stood in his doorway and
called for Zeus and every

3
00:00:05,592 --> 00:00:09,152
god to come and see something
laughable and unbearable.

4
00:00:09,236 --> 00:00:13,396
Aphrodite, he said, had always
scorned him for his lame leg,

5
00:00:13,396 --> 00:00:17,294
and loved Ares because Ares
was handsome and sound of foot.

6
00:00:17,294 --> 00:00:21,071
The gods came — Poseidon,
Apollo and Hermes.

7
00:00:21,149 --> 00:00:23,513
Apollo asked Hermes
whether he would take such

8
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:26,253
chains for a night with golden Aphrodite.

9
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:31,020
Hermes said he would take three times
as many, with every god looking on.

10
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,300
The gods roared with laughter.

11
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:36,375
"Bad deeds do not prosper," one said.

12
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:38,647
"The slow one has caught the swift.

13
00:00:38,689 --> 00:00:44,469
Lame as he is, Hephaestus has caught
the swiftest god on Olympus — by craft."

14
00:00:44,813 --> 00:00:47,085
Only Poseidon did not laugh.
